WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.900
Aliasing means more than one reference can designate the same object.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.760
One pointer may own the object, another may borrow it during a call, another may point into a member, and another may be stored in a container.

3
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:18.940
The object still has one lifetime, but multiple references can make that lifetime harder to reason about.

4
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.860
Borrowed pointers need valid-use windows.

5
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.640
A function may be allowed to read an object only during the call.

6
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.020
A callback may be allowed to retain a pointer only until a related unregister operation.

7
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.920
A parser may borrow input text only until the input buffer is reused.

8
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.020
Those windows should be documented.

9
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.980
Aliases can become stale after cleanup, transfer, resize, or object replacement.

10
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.720
If the owner releases an object, every borrower must stop using it.

11
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:55.860
If a container takes ownership, callers should not continue to mutate the object unless the contract permits it.

12
00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.360
If storage moves, interior aliases need review.

13
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.600
Const-correctness communicates mutation intent.

14
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.340
A pointer to const data tells the callee not to modify the object through that pointer.

15
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:15.640
It does not prove ownership, storage duration, or thread safety, but it makes one part of the lifetime contract clearer.

16
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.480
Retained references require explicit permission.

17
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.500
An API should state whether it copies data, borrows it temporarily, or stores the pointer for later.

18
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:34.200
Without that rule, callers cannot know how long the referenced object must remain alive or who may modify or destroy it.
